{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3307","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3307","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3307\",\"parent_revision\":\"20287056778ed583bca33f7d7b1932f540b95b3e5e0b07af3e79e9a743f26329\",\"root_revision\":\"20287056778ed583bca33f7d7b1932f540b95b3e5e0b07af3e79e9a743f26329\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ngh_client.create_issue_for_item (plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py:1246) computes issue_title = f'{type_map.get(item.item_type.lower(), \\\"feat\\\")}: {item.title}' and mutates item.title to this prefixed form before creating the GitHub issue. None of the other three WorkItemBackend implementations do this: memory_backend.MemoryBackend.create_issue_for_item, sqlite_backend.SQLiteBackend.create_issue_for_item, and beads_backend.BeadsBackend.create_beads_issue_for_item all pass item.title through to their respective creation calls unchanged.\\n\\nThis means the same backlog_add(title='Fix login bug', type='bug') call produces a title of 'fix: Fix login bug' on the GitHub backend but 'Fix login bug' (no prefix) on Beads, SQLite, or in-memory backends \u2014 an arbitrary, backend-dependent difference in behavior for what is conceptually the same operation (BacklogConfig's own WorkItemBackend abstraction promises backend-neutral CRUD). This was just patched around by scoping backlog_add's title field docstring to explicitly describe the GitHub-only behavior (PR #3286), rather than fixing the underlying inconsistency \u2014 the docstring fix stops the tool from misleading callers, but the actual behavioral difference between backends remains.\\n\\nImpact: any workflow, documentation, or duplicate-detection logic that assumes a consistent title shape across backends (e.g. an item migrated from Beads to GitHub, or a cross-backend title-substring search) will see inconsistent results depending solely on which backend is configured via BACKLOG_BACKEND. Not yet assessed: whether the intended fix is to make all backends prefix (matching GitHub's behavior, for consistency) or to remove GitHub's prefixing (matching the other three, and treating the type-derived prefix as purely a GitHub-issue-title convention that back ends need not replicate) \u2014 this is a real design decision, not just a bug fix, and should go through grooming/RT-ICA rather than being decided here.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, while addressing a Codex PR review comment on PR #3286 (backlog_add title docstring), confirmed by reading gh_client.create_issue_for_item vs. memory_backend/sqlite_backend/beads_backend's equivalents\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d9c230c9fd69f1b7f9710c3864aa234f87d09d3f9e25521cea2b844ce0685e3a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5dOA\"}"}